{
  "analysis": "The previous output was truncated, but key facts: no MIPS GCC cross-compiler was found in PATH. The Makefile is a native Linux/X11 clang build and uses doomgeneric_xlib.o, not doomgeneric_img.o. The custom doomgeneric_img.c is at /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c and includes a custom main and __start entry. I need to fully inspect vm.js to understand how it loads doomgeneric_mips, what syscalls/instructions it supports, and whether it expects big-endian or little-endian MIPS.",
  "plan": "Print vm.js in numbered chunks focused on ELF loading, syscall handling, and instruction dispatch. Also inspect the full doomgeneric_img.c and check whether clang can target MIPS.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"elf\\|ELF\\|load\\|syscall\\|read\\|write\\|open\\|exit\\|brk\\|mmap\\|entry\\|endian\\|byteOrder\\|data\" /app/vm.js | head -200\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "nl -ba /app/vm.js | sed -n '1,260p'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "nl -ba /app/vm.js | sed -n '260,560p'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "nl -ba /app/vm.js | sed -n '560,900p'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "nl -ba /app/vm.js | sed -n '900,1300p'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "nl -ba /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c | sed -n '1,260p'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "clang --version; clang -print-targets 2>/dev/null | grep -i mips || true; ls /usr/bin/*mips* 2>/dev/null || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
